CM_ BO_ 37 "TSS3 Corolla uses the legacy steering angle/fraction/rate bit positions inside a 32-byte CAN-FD PDU; exact H firmware and two driving captures support these fields.";
CM_ BO_ 48 "Exact H/F EPS transmits this 32-byte PDU. Driver torque and B6 safety/status gates are target-native recovered fields; byte 7 equals sum(bytes 0..6)+0x38 modulo 256.";
CM_ SG_ 48 STEERING_WHEEL_TORQUE_TRUNC "DID 0x1035 Steering Wheel Torque source, saturating truncation-toward-zero 0.1 Nm view. It can differ from COARSE by one count due to firmware rounding.";
CM_ SG_ 48 STEERING_WHEEL_TORQUE_COARSE "Coarse component of exact physical Steering Wheel Torque reconstruction.";
CM_ SG_ 48 STEERING_WHEEL_TORQUE_FINE "Signed hundredths remainder. Exact torque = COARSE + FINE.";
CM_ SG_ 48 EPS_FAULT_INHIBIT "Selected live EPS fault/inhibit aggregate. Exact F33 maps its recoverable current-unavailability projection to openpilot steerFaultTemporary; this is not an exhaustive fault list or a restart-required latch. H/F policy is separate.";
CM_ SG_ 48 DRIVER_TORQUE_INVALID "Target-native driver-torque invalid/inhibit gate.";
CM_ SG_ 48 EPS_STATUS_B6_BIT1 "Runtime status bit; exact OEM meaning unresolved.";
CM_ SG_ 48 EPS_STATUS_B6_BIT3 "Runtime status bit; exact OEM meaning unresolved.";
CM_ BO_ 129 "Brake-owned TSS3 selected/result/reference PDU. Longitudinal result fields are strong recorder-schema candidates; lateral result fields are independently recovered. B11[4] asserts on FRC request loss.";
CM_ SG_ 129 LONGITUDINAL_RESULT_ID "Strong candidate for recorder 5284 Arbitration result_longitudinal ID; low six bits only. Exact synchronized diagnostic join remains open.";
CM_ SG_ 129 REQUEST_LOSS_STATUS "Live FRC CommunicationControl suppression makes this bit assert while Brake continues 0x081. OEM name and relation to recorder 57D3 remain unresolved.";
CM_ SG_ 129 LATERAL_RESULT_ID "Strong wire join to FFD 5285 Arbitration result_lateral ID; mirrors fresh 0x08A request identity across the retained road corpus.";
CM_ SG_ 129 LATERAL_RESULT_PINION_ANGLE "Selected/result pinion reference. Raw count is approximately the recorder 57DE 0.001-rad unit.";
CM_ SG_ 129 LONGITUDINAL_RESULT_ACCEL "Strong candidate for recorder 57DB Arbitration result Acceleration. Result ID63 nearly passes the 0x08A request through while ID11 diverges under arbitration.";
CM_ BO_ 138 "Unified observed TSS3 request envelope. Carries Toyota recorder 5281 upper longitudinal request, 5280 lower longitudinal request, 5282 lateral request, request-state metadata, a modulo-64 application sequence, and a Toyota Profile-5-style FV4/MAC28 SecOC trailer. Exact placement before/after internal TSS application selection remains unresolved.";
CM_ SG_ 138 REQUEST_STATUS_B4_BIT7 "Retained Camry request-status companion bit. It is set throughout the ordinary request corpus, including every ID11 frame; exact OEM semantic remains unresolved.";
CM_ SG_ 138 DELAYED_HOLD_STATE "Structural Camry hold-state bit: asserted on 198/198 retained delayed-hold frames and clear in every other 3b/3c 0x08A frame. Exact OEM recorder name remains unknown.";
CM_ SG_ 138 LONGITUDINAL_REQUEST_ID_UPPER "Toyota recorder 5281 upper longitudinal request ID in bits7:2. Ordinary Camry DRCC uses ID11 here; unequal-bound evidence resolves this slot as upper.";
CM_ SG_ 138 LONGITUDINAL_ALLOCATION_METHOD_UPPER "Toyota 5281 upper force-allocation method in bits1:0: 0 Engine Only, 1 Engine and Brake 1, 2 Engine and Brake 2, 3 Brake Only.";
CM_ SG_ 138 LONGITUDINAL_REQUEST_ID_LOWER "Toyota recorder 5280 lower longitudinal request ID in bits7:2. Ordinary Camry DRCC uses ID17 here; delayed hold uses ID25.";
CM_ SG_ 138 LONGITUDINAL_ALLOCATION_METHOD_LOWER "Toyota 5280 lower force-allocation method in bits1:0: 0 Engine Only, 1 Engine and Brake 1, 2 Engine and Brake 2, 3 Brake Only.";
CM_ SG_ 138 LONGITUDINAL_REQUEST_ACCEL_UPPER "Toyota recorder 5281 upper acceleration request, signed16 at 0.001 m/s^2/count. Unequal-bound evidence resolves B8:B9 as upper.";
CM_ SG_ 138 LONGITUDINAL_REQUEST_ACCEL_LOWER "Toyota recorder 5280 lower acceleration request, signed16 at 0.001 m/s^2/count. Unequal-bound evidence resolves B11:B12 as lower.";
CM_ SG_ 138 REQUEST_SENTINEL_B13_B14 "Constant 0x7FFF in every retained complete Camry 0x08A frame; surrounding OEM field semantic remains unresolved.";
CM_ SG_ 138 REQUEST_SENTINEL_B16_B17 "Constant 0x7FFF in every retained complete Camry 0x08A frame; surrounding OEM field semantic remains unresolved.";
CM_ SG_ 138 LATERAL_REQUEST_PINION_ANGLE "Recovered Toyota recorder 5282 request pinion reference; controller scale 1024/17870 deg/count is 0.00100012 rad/count.";
CM_ SG_ 138 CRUISE_STATE_MIRROR "B20[7:6] companion state. Steady Camry cruise operation is value 3 and inactive state is 0; it mirrors CRUISE_OPERATING_LATCH apart from bounded transition frames. Individual OEM bit names remain unresolved.";
CM_ SG_ 138 LATERAL_REQUEST_ID "TSS request-side lateral application ID; FFD 5282 calls this TSS request - lateral ID.";
CM_ SG_ 138 CRUISE_REQUEST_ACTIVE "B22[4] request-active state. It mirrors Camry cruise operation apart from bounded transitions and independently separates retained Corolla ACC engaged/disengaged states.";
CM_ SG_ 138 LATERAL_REQUEST_ATTRIBUTE_B23_BIT5 "Real lateral-request attribute: always set in retained ID18/SDG and variable in ID11/LTA-LCA. It correlates strongly with driver steering/torque, but an OEM driver-steering/override name is not yet recovered.";
CM_ SG_ 138 LATERAL_ASSIST_GAIN "Strong structural join to recorder 5282 Steering assist gain at 0.01/count.";
CM_ SG_ 138 LATERAL_DAMPING_GAIN "Bounded structural join to recorder 5282 Damping control gain; zero in both complete Camry drives.";
CM_ SG_ 138 REQUEST_SEQUENCE "Observed modulo-64 application/request publication sequence. This is distinct from the SecOC freshness fragment in B28.";
CM_ SG_ 138 MSG_CNT_LOWER "Low two bits of the SecOC message counter carried in FV4.";
CM_ SG_ 138 RESET_FLAG "Low two bits of the SecOC reset counter carried in FV4.";
CM_ SG_ 138 AUTHENTICATOR "28-bit truncated Toyota Profile-5-style SecOC authenticator occupying B28[3:0] through B31.";

CM_ BO_ 182 "Exact H/F protected final steering-controller target/instruction PDU. Its Target Lateral ID and target steering angle are downstream of the TSS request/result layers; receiver-side fields are defined for analysis.";
CM_ SG_ 182 TARGET_LATERAL_ID "Techstream Target Lateral ID; exact H accepts 1=PCS, 4=LDA, 10=Hands Off LTA, 11=LTA/LCA, 19=PDA. 0 means no request.";
CM_ SG_ 182 TARGET_STEERING_ANGLE "Controller-equivalent scale is exactly 1024/17870 deg/count.";
CM_ SG_ 182 SEQUENCE "Exact H receiver treats this as a modulo-64 sequence counter with effective gap cap 8.";
CM_ BO_ 352 "FRC-origin TSS3 Profile-5 PDU retained as read-only state/evidence. Current evidence does not qualify 0x160 as openpilot longitudinal command ingress; the shared TSS3 control-request plane is 0x08A.";
CM_ SG_ 352 CHECKSUM "Little-endian CRC-16/CCITT over bytes 2..31 followed by Data ID 0x0160 in low-byte/high-byte order, initial value 0xFFFF. The older init=0/Data-ID=0x444A expression is wire-equivalent at this fixed PDU length.";
CM_ SG_ 352 BYTE_4 "Observed state byte. The previous B4:B5 acceleration-request interpretation is not an actuator contract and must not be used for TSS3 longitudinal output.";
CM_ SG_ 352 BYTE_5 "Observed state byte paired with B4 in prior motion-correlation work; no writable longitudinal-command semantic is assigned.";
CM_ SG_ 352 BYTE_12 "Observed state byte; the previous acceleration-command interpretation is withdrawn.";
CM_ SG_ 295 GEAR "Span 2025 Corolla HV directly carries raw 3 while in D; P/R/N/B preserve Toyota hybrid ordinal semantics corroborated by GTS+ P5/P6 Shift Position ordering.";
CM_ SG_ 959 GEAR "Albino 2023 Corolla public route directly observes P=0x80, R=0x40 and D=0x10; Span 2025 Corolla HV independently carries D=0x10. N=0x20 completes the one-hot domain and matches Toyota P5/P6 ordering.";
CM_ SG_ 374 CRUISE_ACTIVE "Legacy field retained for decoding only. Both moving TSS3 Corolla captures keep the old CRUISE_ACTIVE/STATE values inactive; generation-native engagement is 0x08A B22 bit0x10 instead.";

